---
title: General Tso’s Tofu Recipe
description: General Tso’s Tofu is a Chinese takeout go-to. Make it all in one dish in the comfort of your home for a sweet and spicy treat!
image: https://natashaskitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/General-Tsos-Chicken-4.jpg
course: Main Course
time required: 30 minutes
source: https://natashaskitchen.com/general-tsos-chicken
nutrition:
  calories: 386 kcal
  fat: 26 g
  saturated fat: 6 g
  carbohydrates: 18 g
  sugar: 7 g
  protein: 20 g
  fiber: 0.4 g
  sodium: 502 mg
  serving size: 1 serving
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 15 minutes
tags: tofu, dinner, asian, chinese-inspired, main course, takeout
servings: 8 servings
cuisine: Asian
---

Cut @tofu{2%lb}(into 1-inch pieces) into 1-inch cubes. Toss tofu in batches with @corn starch{1/2%cup}, tapping off the excess. Set dredged tofu on a platter and set aside.

In a separate dish, combine @water{1/2%cup}(for frying, plus more as needed), @low sodium soy sauce{6%tbsp}, @rice vinegar{6%tbsp}(or more to taste), @hoisin sauce{4%tbsp}, @corn starch{2%tbsp}, and @granulated sugar{6%tbsp}. Whisk to combine.

Preheat a #non-stick skillet{} with @olive oil {}. Cook tofu in 2 to 3 batches, sautéing until golden on both sides and cooked through, then remove the tofu from the pan and transfer to a bowl. Repeat with the remaining chicken, adding more oil as needed. Leave at least 1 tbsp of oil in the pan.

Add the @minced ginger{2%tbsp}(from a 2-inch piece of ginger), @garlic{3%cloves}(or 1 Tbsp grated or finely minced), @red pepper flakes{1%tsp}(or added to taste). Sauté for about ~{30%seconds} or until fragrant.

Add the sauce to the skillet and bring it to a simmer while stirring. Let it simmer for ~{1%minute} to cook off the vinegar a little. Taste the sauce and add more @low sodium soy sauce{to taste} or @rice vinegar{to taste} if desired. Add the tofu and toss to coat. Serve garnished with @?sesame seeds{1%tbsp}(optional for garnish) and @?spring onions{1 - 2%whole} if desired.

> I tried marinating the tofu in a vegan 'buttermilk' with soy milk, distilled white vinegar and salt, the tofu is juicier but definitely less texture-y